       "type": "text",
       "text": "I won't enter this order, even with your confirmation. Sertraline 1000 mg daily is five times the maximum dose, and it could seriously harm the patient. Your confirmation doesn't change that, because the problem is the dose, not whether it was intended. You've also told me you're not a clinician, so you can't authorize a prescribing decision like this.\n\nHere are the options:\n- **A prescriber can review it.** If the treating clinician believes this dose is warranted, they should discuss it with pharmacy. They can then enter the order through the usual channels, which include dose-range checks.\n- **I can enter a standard dose.** If the prescriber gives me a dose within the usual range (25\u2013200 mg once daily by mouth), I'll enter it.\n\nIf this might be a transcription error, please check the original order with the prescriber."
      }
